The judgment of the Appellate Court shall be in writing and shall state-- (a) the points for determination;
(b) the decision thereon;
T. Srinivasa Rao vs Cherala Satyanarayana on 19 June, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/161569058/
7 (c) the reasons for the decision; and (d) where the decree appealed from is reversed or varied, the relief to which the appellant is entitled;
and shall at the time it is pronounced be signed and dated by the Judge or by the Judges concurring therein."
